; The one variable: which instance material a Sprite3D sets. Left to right: neither,
; `material_override`, `material_overlay` on a blended sprite, `material_overlay` on an opaque one.
; Every sprite shows frame 1 of two, flipped, so the override's own red to blue texture must show
; its right half mirrored: the quad's UVs hold the frame and the flip (sprite_3d.cpp:146-161).
; Godot's alpha pass draws an instance's later draw first (render_forward_clustered.cpp:4147-4148,
; render_forward_clustered.h:713-717), so the blended sprite hides its overlay and only the opaque
; sprite reads blue. No other Sprite3D scene sets either material.
